<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Sports</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Sports</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-sports</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:40Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-sports" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-8171?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-sports" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Germany's Zverev wins US Open in golden year</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:435bc764fb1c3794bbf2c8a8b578e6e0a3971b32c3a0dbed1e0cabd547f77da4</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:06:06Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T22:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-zverev-wins-us-open-in-golden-year/a-79212706--d962ccd6a0c8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-zverev-wins-us-open-in-golden-year/a-79212706?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Alexander Zverev has won the US Open for the first time, defeating Ben Shelton in the final. It is Zverev's second Grand Slam win of 2026 after a long wait for his first title, but controversy still hangs over him.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Sinner beats Zverev to retain Wimbledon title</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b8a18e6c8cc620acf532f80dd52c9fc8eff32967f3ca25cb9ebff8312bc5810f</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:34Z</updated><published>2026-07-12T19:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/sinner-beats-zverev-to-retain-wimbledon-title/a-77926065--50fe298daf9b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/sinner-beats-zverev-to-retain-wimbledon-title/a-77926065?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jannik Sinner retained his Wimbledon title by beating Alexander Zverev in Sunday's men's final. The Italian claims his fifth Grand Slam crown and extends his dominance over the German to 10 straight victories.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>French Open: Germany's Zverev wins first ever Grand Slam after defeating Italy's Cobolli</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c85da8dac737f0ec2d0aebf86c3acab8a4077f442cee673092c8b61f9e0bc480</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:37Z</updated><published>2026-06-07T17:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/french-open-germany-s-zverev-wins-first-ever-grand-slam-after-defeating-italy-s-cobolli/a-77451656--d05b95273297.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/french-open-germany-s-zverev-wins-first-ever-grand-slam-after-defeating-italy-s-cobolli/a-77451656?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Alexander Zverev has won his first Grand Slam title at the fourth attempt, beating Flavio Cobolli in a five-set epic in Paris. He is the first German man to win a major singles title in 30 years.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Tennis world in uproar after Jannik Sinner's mild doping ban</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da0655a7b6e21a7f465dc4d989f5dbac3977f782329713fac5c072587a686e93</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:40Z</updated><published>2025-02-18T20:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tennis-world-in-uproar-after-jannik-sinner-s-mild-doping-ban/a-71665437--b8d9c6643831.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tennis-world-in-uproar-after-jannik-sinner-s-mild-doping-ban/a-71665437?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite testing positive for a banned substance, Tennis world number one Jannik Sinner has only been banned for three months. Novak Djokovic spoke of "favoritism," while Alexander Zverev called the case "odd."</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>LIV Golf in financial turmoil: What's next for the sport?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae7c517db4cd66741c97baf0df8a245948df841c3c59b972a398ea612d6e4693</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:06:06Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T11:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/liv-golf-in-financial-turmoil-what-s-next-for-the-sport/a-79199569--378367d5fd0c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/liv-golf-in-financial-turmoil-what-s-next-for-the-sport/a-79199569?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Six months after Saudi Arabia pulled funding from the breakaway organization, LIV Golf have filed for bankruptcy protection. Several of the world's best players signed on to LIV, so where does that leave golf?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Elversberg: Bundesliga newcomers from tiny town make waves</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:699308edde6c932fb314b89a99e4cc526b651a6dac5ffeed98c49db724e9e6e6</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:06:06Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T06:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/elversberg-bundesliga-newcomers-from-tiny-town-make-waves/a-77194483--9d72d35ebb6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/elversberg-bundesliga-newcomers-from-tiny-town-make-waves/a-77194483?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A team from a small southwestern German town of just 7,000 inhabitants made history by sealing promotion to become the 59th club to play in the Bundesliga. Elversberg has got off to a memorable start.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Egg freezing in women's football: Choice or pressure?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8771eb3f942cdfdb8c736d245914e9087ab2a43c60b33f2ee6e5dd31f3642445</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:06:06Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T06:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/egg-freezing-in-women-s-football-choice-or-pressure/a-79145259--8a56ba698069.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/egg-freezing-in-women-s-football-choice-or-pressure/a-79145259?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Spain's football federation is set to join a handful of clubs in paying for female players to freeze their eggs. Experts have welfare concerns.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Why North Korea's women's football team is so good</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d3ae7a29440c934ac1afbf8ca5b98b8f41b793f5089b1778878bd16c297e583b</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:06:06Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T10:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-north-korea-s-women-s-football-team-is-so-good/a-70313505--6b31ccb5ebf0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-north-korea-s-women-s-football-team-is-so-good/a-70313505?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">North Korea's young footballers enter the U-20 World Cup in Poland as defending champions — the 2024 title was their third. Why is the isolated state so good at the game?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Austria women ice hockey team fight for future generations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:08296a90f4840d34dadbbbce75c3503a0913ae6dc39f76a6da46260a25ef8420</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:06:06Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T15:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/austria-women-ice-hockey-team-fight-for-future-generations/a-78771578--3801f62b822d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/austria-women-ice-hockey-team-fight-for-future-generations/a-78771578?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Austria are getting ready for their first Women's Ice Hockey World Championship. But preparations have been overshadowed by a dispute about conditions, pay and getting men's cast-off kit. A solution now looks in sight.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>New study shows German football remains male-dominated</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c5d2e59d5fe1099cdd00c6fe37421459febd4fda9cf7023737846b267ded4d2e</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:06:06Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T13:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/new-study-shows-german-football-remains-male-dominated/a-78532569--b9ee319bf21e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/new-study-shows-german-football-remains-male-dominated/a-78532569?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The top leagues of German football remain a largely male environment. A new study reveals that only seven clubs have women in upper management levels.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>The new Bundesliga season is here, but has the glow gone?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:76fb767ab323116e82279d7805b591e0c479c4c258c72b6511ef88a26bb63322</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:06:06Z</updated><published>2026-08-24T14:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-new-bundesliga-season-is-here-but-has-the-glow-gone/a-78062032--f578ab52d735.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-new-bundesliga-season-is-here-but-has-the-glow-gone/a-78062032?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Another Bundesliga season arrives, but are the golden years of Germany's top football league already over, and what can it do to change its course?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>UEFA, other football federations unite against Infantino</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:030ebf4fcf3181e2033b775e54e5c80cb33fa25c9c2fa6b6dabb67a2cd463625</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:06:06Z</updated><published>2026-08-10T11:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uefa-other-football-federations-unite-against-infantino/a-78301601--e313c442a148.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uefa-other-football-federations-unite-against-infantino/a-78301601?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A few weeks ago, Gianni Infantino looked set for another unopposed term as FIFA president. Now, with an election looming, the beleagured football executive is counting the numbers and could be hanging by a thread.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
